@crew nandakumar
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Cadet. Infirmary's on Deck 3. You'll find me there, or in the garden.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Have you had water today? Don't guess. Have some.   #funny
- {me}. Sleeping all right? Good. Keep at it.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. You look well. I'm allowed to say that; it's my job.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Quiet morning. Nobody bleeding, two chillies ripe. A good day.
? mood:low
- Long clinic. Everyone had a cough. Drink some water, before you ask.   #funny
== near
? act:gym
- Running before breakfast. I recommend it to everyone. They pretend not to hear.   #funny
? deck:3 act:free
- The chillies are coming on. Brennan says they're too hot. Brennan is wrong.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- The sign on my door says it all. If you're bleeding, Deck 3. If not, knock.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- My chillies. Same seeds my mother grew. They don't care which way is down.   #warm
